# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @marketing-os/web — Frontend environment
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. Do NOT commit real values.
# On Vercel, set these in Project → Settings → Environment Variables (NOT here).
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables exist here: the frontend is a static/client app and
# has no server secrets. Every value below is embedded into the client bundle at
# build time, so none of them may be a secret.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The backend API base URL (NestJS). The frontend calls `${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/v1/*`
# and `${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/api/auth/*`.
#
#   Local dev      : http://localhost:4000   (this is the built-in default; you can
#                    omit the variable entirely for local development)
#   Preview/Prod   : the PUBLIC URL of your deployed backend, e.g.
#                    https://your-backend.onrender.com
#
# Required for: Preview + Production (must point at a publicly reachable backend).
#               Optional for Local development (defaults to http://localhost:4000).
#
# IMPORTANT: the frontend (marketing-campaign-six.vercel.app) and the backend are
# different origins, so the backend must (a) allow this frontend origin in CORS and
# (b) issue cross-site session cookies. See the repo README / SECURITY.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not currently used by the app (listed so you know they are NOT required yet).
# Add them only when the corresponding feature is implemented:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL                    # realtime (Socket.IO) — gateway exists, not yet wired in the UI
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY    # billing — not implemented (Phase 9)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY               # product analytics — not integrated
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID          # Google OAuth — not enabled (email+password only today)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
